From 92db74473d75d80546fbbeb81a250844ba6043a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 08:00:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] obexd: remove the part of a push the sender disconnected in

A client that ends its session while a PUT is still running sends
DISCONNECT without ABORT; obexd's own client does so when its session
is removed. cmd_disconnect() then makes DISCONNECT the session's
current command, and when the transport goes, os_reset_session() marks
the transfer aborted but no longer finds a PUT, so the part received
is not removed. It stays in the receive folder under the name of a
received file.

Reset an open transfer in cmd_disconnect() while its command is still
known. The transfer is then reported failed as before, and the part
of an unfinished PUT is removed as after an ABORT.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 obexd/src/obex.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/obexd/src/obex.c b/obexd/src/obex.c
index 370bfac..3f7d40a 100644
--- a/obexd/src/obex.c
+++ b/obexd/src/obex.c
@@ -305,6 +305,12 @@ static void cmd_disconnect(GObex *obex, GObexPacket *req, void *user_data)
 
 	print_event(G_OBEX_OP_DISCONNECT, -1);
 
+	/* A transfer still open ends here: reset it while its command is
+	 * known, or os_reset_session() later finds DISCONNECT and keeps the
+	 * part of an unfinished PUT. */
+	if (os->object)
+		os_reset_session(os);
+
 	os->cmd = G_OBEX_OP_DISCONNECT;
 
 	os_set_response(os, 0);
